# Prelude — Plugin capability shape (R11 plugin-only wave, 2026-09-01).
#
# `use plugin: Plugin` inside a shim atom licenses that shim to call
# the compiler-resolved FFI intrinsics:
#
#   plugin.get(sym: String) -> <declared-signature>
#   plugin.send(recv, sel: String, args...) -> <declared-signature>
#   plugin.class_send(cls: String, sel: String, args...) -> <declared-signature>
#
# The runtime linker (F76) refuses to fill this slot outside modules
# carrying a top-level `def plugin:` record marker. Trust boundary
# enforced at env construction, not parse time.
#
# Method surface is compile-time-resolved: the string argument to
# .get / .send / .class_send names a foreign entry declared inside
# the enclosing `def plugin:` body's nested `foreign "libname":`
# sections. The resolver (B5) substitutes each call with a typed
# :ffi-call node using the signature declared for that foreign
# entry. Because signatures vary per foreign entry, Plugin declares
# no method shape here at v1.0 — B5 supplies the shape from the
# foreign declaration.
#
# Cross-plugin symbol access is impossible by construction (B6):
# each `Plugin` capability handle resolves ONLY against the
# enclosing plugin's own `foreign` sections, never another
# plugin's.
#
# See spec §1.12, §7.2.1 R7, decisions-frozen-2026-09-01-plugin-only.md,
# and [[corvid-plugin-shape]].

def Plugin:
    -> ready
